  "question": {
    "text": "Considering only the principal values of inverse trigonometric functions, the number of positive real values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Dv7Mb",
      "text": "More than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "55Nns",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Ym4VI",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mAISK",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p>Now, differentiating the above function we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>;</mo><mo> </mo><mo>∀</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>→</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></munder><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></math> is monotonically increasing for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and the range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> has exactly one solution for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
